-- title:
--   Homothety of paired QM period lattices versus Fuchsian orbits
-- statement:
--   Fix a natural number $N \neq 0$ and primes $q, q'$ with $q \nmid N$, $q' \nmid N$ and $q' \neq q$, and rationals $a, b$ such that `IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b q q'` holds for the quaternion algebra $B = \mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q}, a, b]$: namely $0 < a$ or $0 < b$, and for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ the completed algebra $B \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_v$ is a division algebra exactly when $q \in v$ or $q' \in v$. Let $\Lambda \subseteq B$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule that is a maximal order (it contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, spans $B$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, is finitely generated, and is maximal among such submodules containing it), let $N$ be squarefree, and let $R \subseteq \Lambda$ be an Eichler order of level $N$, i.e. $R = \Lambda_1 \cap \Lambda_2$ for maximal orders $\Lambda_1, \Lambda_2$ with $[\Lambda_1 : R] = N$. Let $\iota : B \to M_2(\mathbb{R})$ be an injective $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra homomorphism. Let $J'$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $B$ with $\Lambda \subseteq J'$, $\Lambda J' \subseteq J'$, $N J' \subseteq \Lambda$, additive index $[J' : \Lambda] = N^2$, and such that for $x \in \Lambda$ one has $x \in R$ if and only if $J' x \subseteq J'$. For $\tau, \tau'$ in the upper half-plane, writing $L_\sigma(M) = \{(\iota y)\binom{\tau}{1} : y \in M\}$ for the image of a submodule $M$ under $y \mapsto (\iota y)$ complexified and applied to $(\sigma, 1)^{\mathsf{T}}$, the assertion is: there exists $c \in \mathbb{C}$, $c \neq 0$, with $c\, L_\tau(\Lambda) = L_{\tau'}(\Lambda)$ and $c\, L_\tau(J') = L_{\tau'}(J')$ if and only if there exists $\gamma$ in `fuchsianGroup R ι` — the intersection of the image under $\iota$ of the subgroup of $B^\times$ generated by the units $u$ satisfying `IsUnitOf R u` with the kernel of the determinant — such that $\gamma \cdot \tau = \tau'$.
--
--   This is the lattice-theoretic description of the points of the Shimura curve of level $N$ attached to the indefinite quaternion algebra ramified exactly at $q$ and $q'$: homothety classes of the pair of period lattices of a quaternionic multiplication abelian surface with its $\Gamma_0(N)$-type structure correspond to orbits of the Fuchsian group of the Eichler order $R$. It is used in the construction of coarse and fine moduli interpretations of the uniformised Hecke curve and in the comparison of period maps with algebraic charts.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_QuaternionAlgebra_IsEichlerOrder_exists_smul_qmPeriodLattice_pair_eq_iff_exists_fuchsianGroup_smul_eq.lean

